{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Prototype as Playable Question.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Prototype as Playable Question.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"prototype as playable question prototype as playable question","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Prototype as Playable Question.md","fileName":"Prototype as Playable Question.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Prototype as Playable Question","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 00:27\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Iterative Game Design Cycle]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Iterative Game Design Cycle","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Prototype as Playable Question.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Prototype as Playable Question.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"prototype as playable question prototype as playable question","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Prototype as Playable Question.md","fileName":"Prototype as Playable Question.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Prototype as Playable Question","heading":"Prototype as Playable Question","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A prototype is most useful when it poses a specific question that can be answered through play. Its features and fidelity should be limited to what is necessary to expose that uncertainty.\n\nTreating the artifact as a question prevents polish from masquerading as knowledge. A narrow prototype can be discarded after the answer changes the design, while an unfocused miniature game makes it difficult to know which assumption a test confirmed or challenged.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Iterative Game Design Cycle","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Prototype as Playable Question.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Prot